<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_Process_Acquisti" targetNamespace="http://corso-processi.local/apqc">
  <bpmn:process id="Process_Acquisti" name="4.2.3 Select suppliers and develop/maintain contracts" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Category 4.0 Manage Supply Chain for Physical Products
Process Group 4.2 Procure materials and services (10216)
Process 4.2.3 Select suppliers and develop/maintain contracts (10278)

Definizione APQC: Evaluating supplier options to select the most effective and efficient suppliers. Validate selected suppliers. Establish and manage supplier contracts.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 4.0 Manage Supply Chain for Physical Products (K012577).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/03-acquisti/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_1">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_PM" name="Procurement/Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Legal" name="Ufficio Legale">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start" name="Fabbisogno di approvvigionamento identificato">

      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="T1" name="4.2.3.1 Select suppliers (10288)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Evaluating the pros and cons of various suppliers. Choose the most appropriate and cost-effective suppliers on the basis of their material quality, delivery schedules, and costs.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 4.0 Manage Supply Chain for Physical Products (K012577).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/03-acquisti/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T2" name="4.2.3.2 Certify and validate suppliers (10289)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Validating the supply sources, and provide certification as an official supplier.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 4.0 Manage Supply Chain for Physical Products (K012577).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/03-acquisti/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T3" name="4.2.3.3 Negotiate contract terms (10290)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Attivita' 4.2.3.3 Negotiate and establish contracts (10290) — fase di negoziazione (in SAEM/versione astratta, la negoziazione e l'approvazione legale sono rappresentate come due task separati sulla stessa Activity).

Definizione APQC: Legally binding suppliers with the company. Negotiate contracts individually with all the suppliers that include the promised material delivery, the delivery dates and duration, etc.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 4.0 Manage Supply Chain for Physical Products (K012577).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/03-acquisti/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T4" name="4.2.3.3 Establish and approve contract (10290)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Attivita' 4.2.3.3 Negotiate and establish contracts (10290) — fase di approvazione legale (in SAEM/versione astratta, la negoziazione e l'approvazione legale sono rappresentate come due task separati sulla stessa Activity).

Definizione APQC: Legally binding suppliers with the company. Negotiate contracts individually with all the suppliers that include the promised material delivery, the delivery dates and duration, etc.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 4.0 Manage Supply Chain for Physical Products (K012577).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/03-acquisti/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T5" name="4.2.3.4 Manage contracts (10291)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Keeping contracts up-to-date with routine evaluation. Maintain order and discipline with the contracts in order to avoid any loss of information and mishaps.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 4.0 Manage Supply Chain for Physical Products (K012577).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/03-acquisti/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End" name="Contratto attivo a sistema">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_6</bpmn:incoming>

    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="Start" targetRef="T1" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="T1" targetRef="T2" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="T2" targetRef="T3" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="T3" targetRef="T4" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" sourceRef="T4" targetRef="T5" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" sourceRef="T5" targetRef="End" />
  </bpmn:process>
